# Breakdown widget — 5 design suggestions

The Breakdown widget groups instances by a field (enum / user / label) and shows
the counts. Today `chart` = `"bar" | "pie"`. Below are 5 distinct directions —
each is a new `chart`/`variant` value (#5 also adds one config field).

All share the existing config: `conceptId`, `conditions[]` + `match`, `groupBy`,
`sort` (count / label / field-order), `values`, `maxGroups → "Other"`.

---

## 1. Ranked bars (horizontal)

Sorted descending, one row per group: label · bar · count · share. Beats the
current vertical bars when labels are long or there are many groups (vertical
axis truncates "Negotiation" → "Nego…"). The everyday default.

```
┌─ Deals by Stage ──────────────────────────────┐
│                                                │
│  Negotiation  ████████████████████   42   35% │
│  Qualified    ██████████████         29   24% │
│  Discovery    █████████              19   16% │
│  Proposal     ███████                14   12% │
│  Closed Won   █████                  10    8% │
│  Closed Lost  ███                     6    5% │
│                                                │
│                               Total: 120 deals │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

`chart: "bars-h"` — reuses `values` (count / percent / both), `sort`, `maxGroups`.

---

## 2. Donut with center total

The pie, upgraded: thicker ring, total in the hole, legend with swatch · count ·
share to the right. Reads as a KPI ("60 open") and a composition at once.

```
┌─ Tickets by Priority ─────────────────────────┐
│                                                │
│        ╭─────────╮          ● Urgent   18  30% │
│      ╭─╯ ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ ╰─╮        ● High      22  37%│
│     │ ▓▓▓       ▓▓ │        ● Medium    14  23%│
│     │ ▓▓   60    ▓ │        ● Low        6  10%│
│     │ ▓▓  open   ▓ │                           │
│      ╰─╮ ▓▓▓▓▓▓ ╭─╯                            │
│        ╰─────────╯                             │
│                                                │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

`chart: "donut"` — center shows `total` (or a chosen agg later); legend uses `values`.

---

## 3. Composition bar (100% stacked)

One full-width segmented bar = share of total, legend underneath. The most
compact form — fits a wide, short tile (h=1). Great for "what's the mix" when
exact per-group counts matter less than proportions.

```
┌─ Pipeline Composition ────────────────────────┐
│                                                │
│  ████████████▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▒▒▒▒▒▒░░░░░░░░░░          │
│                                                │
│  ██ New 35%   ▓▓ Active 25%   ▒▒ Won 18%       │
│  ░░ Lost 22%                                   │
│                                                │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

`chart: "stacked"` — single bar; `values` toggles inline % vs counts in legend.

---

## 4. Breakdown table

Text-first, precise, sortable. Columns: group · count · share · mini-trend ·
Δ vs prior period. Borrows `delta` ("7d"/"30d") from the Metric widget so each
row says not just "how many" but "which way". Best when numbers must be exact.

```
┌─ Leads by Source ─────────────────────────────┐
│  Source        Count   Share   Trend    Δ 7d   │
│  ────────────────────────────────────────────  │
│  Referral        48     32%   ▁▂▃▅▆█    +12%   │
│  Organic         37     25%   ▃▃▄▄▅▅     +4%   │
│  Paid Ads        29     19%   █▆▅▃▂▁    −18%   │
│  Outbound        21     14%   ▂▃▃▄▄▅     +6%   │
│  Event           15     10%   ▁▁▂▂▃▃     +2%   │
│  ────────────────────────────────────────────  │
│  Total          150    100%                     │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

`chart: "table"` — adds optional `delta` ("off"/"7d"/"30d") + `showTrend`.

---

## 5. Cross-tab heatmap (two-dimensional)

The one new *capability*: break down by **two** fields at once. Rows = `groupBy`,
columns = a new `splitBy`, cells = count shaded by magnitude. Answers "which
owner is stuck in which stage" — impossible with any single-axis chart.

```
┌─ Deals: Stage × Owner ────────────────────────┐
│               Alice   Bob   Cara   Dan         │
│  Discovery    ░  3    ▒  6   ░  2   ░  4        │
│  Qualified    ▓  9    █ 12   ▒  5   ░  3        │
│  Proposal     ▒  4    ░  2   ▓  8   ▒  5        │
│  Negotiation  █ 11    ▓  7   ▒  6   ░  1        │
│  Closed Won   ░  2    ░  3   ▒  5   ░  2        │
│                                                │
│   ░ low   ▒ med   ▓ high   █ peak              │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

`chart: "matrix"` + new `splitBy` (second enum/user field). Cells optionally
show count, percent-of-row, or percent-of-total.

---

## At a glance

| # | Variant          | New config            | Best for                          |
|---|------------------|-----------------------|-----------------------------------|
| 1 | Ranked bars      | `chart:"bars-h"`      | many groups / long labels (default)|
| 2 | Donut + total    | `chart:"donut"`       | KPI + mix in one glance           |
| 3 | Composition bar  | `chart:"stacked"`     | wide short tile, proportions only |
| 4 | Breakdown table  | `chart:"table"`,`delta`| exact numbers + direction         |
| 5 | Cross-tab heatmap| `chart:"matrix"`,`splitBy`| two-dimensional breakdown      |

#1–#3 are pure recharts/render swaps. #4 reuses the Metric `delta` machinery.
#5 is the only one needing a query/aggregation change (group by two keys).
